// moving parts. The app merges every mesh of a landmark per material right after build(), so anything that moves is built
// into its own Object3D that is NOT part of the returned group: on the first frame after placement it is added next to the
// landmark group (same parent, same transform, copied every frame) and driven by HOOKS.frame. Kept out of the group it is
// also invisible to the app's ground-plan hull (lower 25 m), so moving cabins never hide real buildings. Without HOOKS (the
// offline kits) the parts are frozen at a representative pose and merged with the rest.
